A||||6||Gokart||Hot enough?||||1
Z||000000||Gokart||11-12-1999||07:27 PM||||Don't know if I should be concerned or not, but my temp gauge barely reaches the 1/4 mark. Asked for a hotter thermostat at parts store, but didn't make much difference. Should gauge read at least half way? Wonder if a sensor needs replacing? Little help! TIA||||reg||1
Z||000001||Greg Piet||11-12-1999||07:56 PM||||your gauge may just be out of calibration, the temp sensor may need to be replaced to get the gauge working more accurately.  In my 85 SE (2.8 v6) it sits around 180, but then again i replaced my temp sensor when i first got the car.  Not sure if this will work, but if the car thinks its cold, putting the car in diagnostic mode while running i think the check engine light will flash very fast, while if it is all warmed up it should flash at about 1 blink a sec.  ( I know when mine is cold it does this)||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||11-13-1999||05:54 AM||||Most thermostats are 180 or 190, fan goes on just past 220. You are just right. Don't worry.||||reg||1
Z||000003||kornholio||11-13-1999||01:20 PM||||Gokart,<BR>I went through the same thing just last week.  I changed the thermostat because I though it was faulty.  When the engine is warmed up, it still reads at the 1/4 mark with the new thermostat.  I never get the check engine light for this.<P>Where is the temp sensor located and is it expensive?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Greg Piet||11-13-1999||03:43 PM||||In the V6 the temp sensor is right next to the fan switch on the engine.<BR>The fan switch is on the right of the motor with one wire coming out of it.  the wire is green with a white line on it The sensor next to it is the one the computer uses.<BR>For a map with descriptions go to: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/sensors.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/sensors.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gokart||11-13-1999||05:43 PM||||Even though I didn't get a "check engine light" I plugged my code reader in anyways and got nothing but 12, so I guess I shouldn't worry about it. Especially since I'm usually worried about it OVERheating.||||reg||1
Z||000006||hefty||11-14-1999||02:30 PM||||I got my '87 GT with an aftermarket elec. fan. The previous owner left it on all the time. I usualy run 1/4 mark all the time. I leave the fan off till I hit this mark. What temp. should engine run at ? I heard engine damage can occur arount 210-220. Is that true ?||||reg||1
